  "summary": "Leaders: euRobotics (ERF, ERL, ERW, awards) and Planète Sciences (Coupe de France de Robotique, Eurobot) structure the European and French event scene; ICRA 2026 Vienna, RSS 2027 Athens and RoboCup 2027 Nuremberg bring top academic competitions to Europe.\nMoney: prizes are modest but real (KUKA Innovation Award 20k EUR + robot loan, Hello Tomorrow 200k EUR grand prize, i-Lab grants); industrial demand concentrates at trade fairs (HANNOVER MESSE, automatica, LogiMAT, SIDO).\nRobot-learning fit: ICRA challenges (LeHome, REAL-I, AgiBot World), euROBIN hackathons and the LeRobot worldwide hackathon match the 42AI wedge and favour software-strong teams.\nLocal Paris anchors: ROSCon France (Paris 2026), Apérobot and Women in Robotics Paris meetups give low-cost visibility and access to mechanics/electronics mentors.\nBest entry point for 42AI: re-host the next LeRobot hackathon site at 42, enter the Coupe de France de Robotique 2027 (May, La Roche-sur-Yon) and submit a talk/demo to ROSCon France.",
